{"type":"standard","title":"Jimi language (Cameroon)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jimi language (Cameroon)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q56288","titles":{"canonical":"Jimi_language_(Cameroon)","normalized":"Jimi language (Cameroon)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jimi language (Cameroon)</span></span>"},"pageid":16001126,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1139940880","tid":"3f3b192b-aee3-11ed-9a7e-109b9914f00b","timestamp":"2023-02-17T16:50:56Z","description":"Chadic language spoken in Cameroon","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimi_language_(Cameroon)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimi_language_(Cameroon)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimi_language_(Cameroon)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jimi_language_(Cameroon)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimi_language_(Cameroon)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Jimi_language_(Cameroon)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimi_language_(Cameroon)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jimi_language_(Cameroon)"}},"extract":"Jimi (Djimi), also known as Jimjimən and 'Um Falin, is a Chadic language spoken in Cameroon in Far North Province on the Nigerian border in and around Bourrha. Dialects are Djimi, Jimo, Malabu, Wadi, and Zumo.","extract_html":"<p><b>Jimi</b> (Djimi), also known as <b>Jimjimən</b> and<i> 'Um Falin</i>, is a Chadic language spoken in Cameroon in Far North Province on the Nigerian border in and around Bourrha. Dialects are Djimi, Jimo, Malabu, Wadi, and Zumo.</p>"}